WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.427
There is no single best vector database for every RAG project.

00:00:04.427 --> 00:00:14.757
For a notebook or small class project, NumPy, FAISS, or Chroma may be the best choice because they are simple and

00:00:14.757 --> 00:00:22.967
transparent. For a small application that needs persistence and filtering, Chroma or Qdrant may be practical.

00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:30.617
If the organization already depends heavily on PostgreSQL, pgvector may reduce architectural complexity.

00:00:31.308 --> 00:00:40.585
For managed cloud deployment, teams may evaluate services such as Pinecone or hosted versions of Qdrant, Weaviate,

00:00:40.585 --> 00:00:48.760
or Zilliz. The decision should consider document volume, update frequency, metadata filtering, latency, security, cost,

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.975
backup requirements, and team skills.

00:00:51.975 --> 00:00:58.390
Do not choose a database only because it appears frequently in tutorials.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:06.140
The storage layer should support the needs of the application and the organization.
